 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time complexity:** Sampling is $O(N_{patch})$ where $N_{patch}$ is the number of rays in the patch. The overhead of coordinate generation is negligible compared to ray casting. [G]
-- **Memory complexity:** $O(N_{patch})$ to store ray origins and directions. For $192 \times 192$, this is 36,864 rays [S1, unofficial].
